 with $X' = \{i,j\}$. Since the $\mathcal L_{B,X}$ with $|X| = 1$ and the $\mathcal S^0_{B,i,\emptyset}$ have been eliminated, and all the $\mathcal L'$ and $\mathcal D'$ generators evaluate to zero by Lemmas~\ref{lemma:vanishingGenus2} and~\ref{lemma:D'vanishingGenus2}, we deduce from Lemma~\ref{lemma:intersectionTableH11xH4} that the only three sets of generators that do not pull back to zero are $\mathcal S^0_{B_1,\{i,j\},\emptyset}$, $\mathcal S^1_{B_2,\emptyset,\{i,j\}}$ and $\mathcal L_{B_3,\{i,j\}}$. Their pullbacks have the same first Künneth components if and only if $B_1 = B_2 = B_3$, and in this case their second Künneth components in $H^4(\overline{\mathcal M}_{1,\{t,i,j\}}) = H^4(\overline{\mathcal M}_{1,3})$ can be explicitly shown to be linearly independent using \texttt{admcycles}. Moreover, the first Künneth component of each forms a basis of $H^{11}(\overline{\mathcal M}_{1,([n]\setminus ij) \cup s})$ when running over all $B \subseteq [n] \setminus ij$. 
Hence, we conclude $s^0_{B,X, \varnothing} = s^1_{B, \varnothing, Y} = \ell_{B, X} = 0$ for $|X| = 2$ or $|Y| = 2$ and any $B$.

\item We pull back to  

  \ensuremath{\mathord{\vcenter{\hbox{ 
